md='''# Additive B judgment: source scope and two prerequisite interfaces

Original FIRST remains exact: `02e14f0f82dfaf08ba13686c1aa4140e139abc0f2d09fefbf24dd08591f680fe`.

## 1. Source applicability: KEEP eleven targets

I independently read the actual joint [Sek-I curriculum](https://bildungsserver.berlin-brandenburg.de/fileadmin/bbb/unterricht/rahmenlehrplaene/Rahmenlehrplanprojekt/amtliche_Fassung/Teil_C_Chemie_2015_11_10.pdf) at printed32/34/36/37/40/42/43/44 and [upper-stage curriculum](https://bildungsserver.berlin-brandenburg.de/fileadmin/bbb/unterricht/rahmenlehrplaene/gymnasiale_oberstufe/curricula/2022/Teil_C_RLP_GOST_2022_Chemie.pdf) at17/19/21/50, including page images and columns.

All eleven existing whole competencies are applicable to these two CrossStage LK target scopes under the owner’s all-authored-topics interim policy. The lower-stage foundations and organic contents support most; the upper introductory themes support the complete structural/isomer/EPA competences. Introductory school selection, italic extensions and lower-stage differentiation remain official qualifications. This does not make every theme an official universal Sek-II obligation or claim a persisted selection/full source union.

**Minimal scope correction: eleven existing leaf targets in each view,22 placements,0 new atoms.** My earlier tentative support-only option is superseded for these two scopes by this primary-source-informed finding. FIRST and dissent remain intact. Seven exposed missing IDs and four deeper IDs still do not mean eleven immediate blockers or eleven fresh science quotas.

## 2. Prerequisite necessity: two exact REVISE findings

- `81373fb7-2a4a-5b2c-acd0-b4e775acaa65`: replace full ester prior `70b34ae7-4481-590c-9a02-516464750832` with existing `8d4ef102-e6a6-4d2e-bb6b-e707d3f2e566` (reaction/product-identity evidence) and `13d4f336-ab16-54a7-9479-c920b458f385` (safe laboratory practice); retain its existing orientation edge. I read the entire current profile and q3-a/b/c/d/e whole materials, including named Fe/SCN method and raw fixture. The executable operator uses an inorganic1:1 reaction, not ester synthesis/property mastery. Ester planning and article critique supply their reaction/species context.
- `91cd4728-b811-562a-970b-18b81dfb4bdf`: replace full constitutional-alcohol-isomer prior `e9b61d96-a271-5e69-b872-8c463f822be1` with existing `eb7537dd-d11b-50e9-a6d7-51a78e96fc4e` (intermolecular forces). Actual current cases compare given methanol/ethane and a longer straight alcohol chain; they need interaction reasoning, not enumeration of isomers.

All three proposed narrower priors are already actual targets in both views; no reverse prerequisite path creates a cycle. I discarded `11bea` after reading its whole P: it would impose unnecessary redox half-equation performance on the non-redox Fe/SCN case. No substitute goal is declared equivalent merely by title.

The eleven targets remain independently intended learning goals even when these two edges are corrected. Adding them and correcting two edges answer different questions.

Actual task arithmetic was checked: open A/B balances0/0; without feed−6/0 at that instant. Fe/SCN nominal80µM; conservative upper86.67µM, positive residual bounds893.33µM Fe and305.33µM SCN. Practical8P and interpretation12P remain distinct; no performed experiment is claimed.

## State and limits

Current L6 `d389cd002b082874845802d4bd9272890050864fe52f5d838388afe9ae581a3d` differs from this review’s earlier selected inputs only by removal of DE-HB from9fef applicability. BB/BE roles and scientific bodies remain unchanged. Neither scope correction nor prerequisite correction is applied by this reviewer.

No new P approval, formal NativeD, source-union pass, global validation, M7 or human approval is asserted. Original review history remains exact.
'''
